WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.732
The purpose of the NAAC AQAR portal is to collect clean, validated data from university institutes for submission to NAAC, the National Assessment and Accreditation Council.

2
00:00:10.732 --> 00:00:22.767
At Symbiosis, the portal supports forty-three institutes through five steps: institute selection, staff verification, metric and CSV validation, supporting document upload, and final submission.

3
00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:26.924
QMB then reviews the records and requests corrections where needed.

4
00:00:27.624 --> 00:00:32.415
First, the coordinator selects an institute from the list mapped in Google Sheets.

5
00:00:32.415 --> 00:00:38.200
In step two, the portal checks the authorised email address and shared passcode for that institute.

6
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.362
The details shown here are fictional.

7
00:00:40.362 --> 00:00:46.205
After verification, the coordinator can continue with submission and access the institute dashboard.

8
00:00:46.905 --> 00:00:55.618
In step three, the coordinator selects a criterion and metric, downloads its predefined template, completes the data, and uploads the CSV.

9
00:00:55.618 --> 00:00:59.975
Google Apps Script defines the expected columns and validation rules.

10
00:00:59.975 --> 00:01:04.521
If the metric applies but there is no data, the coordinator chooses Nil.

11
00:01:04.521 --> 00:01:08.120
If the metric does not apply, they choose Not Applicable.

12
00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:13.757
In step four, supporting documents are uploaded to a dedicated Google Drive folder.

13
00:01:13.757 --> 00:01:16.909
The coordinator has editing access during this stage.

14
00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:21.430
In step five, they review the details and accept the declaration checkboxes.

15
00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:29.520
After final submission, the coordinator’s folder access changes from editing to viewing, and the submission is available for QMB review.

16
00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:35.681
The institute dashboard shows submission history, review status, and requested corrections.

17
00:01:35.681 --> 00:01:41.742
Coordinators can identify approved records and items returned for CSV or supporting-document updates.

18
00:01:41.742 --> 00:01:50.624
These numbers are demonstration data: thirty-six approved, nine pending, four requiring correction, and two not submitted, out of fifty-one metrics.

19
00:01:50.624 --> 00:01:53.625
They are not actual institute performance results.

20
00:01:54.325 --> 00:02:01.434
Authorised QMB reviewers use the admin dashboard to inspect submissions and mark them approved or requiring correction.

21
00:02:01.434 --> 00:02:08.125
The interface also includes institute filters, criterion summaries, a status tracker, and report export options.

22
00:02:08.125 --> 00:02:11.530
All figures here are synthetic and internally consistent.

23
00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:19.834
For example, fifteen hundred approved, four hundred fifty pending, and one hundred fifty redo records total twenty-one hundred submissions.

24
00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:23.061
A completed submission moves to QMB review.

25
00:02:23.061 --> 00:02:30.936
If changes are needed, the institute sees the redo request in its dashboard, makes the requested correction, and resubmits for review.

26
00:02:30.936 --> 00:02:33.169
Approval completes the current review.

27
00:02:33.169 --> 00:02:39.339
The portal also preserves earlier versions, so a correction does not mean losing the previous submission.

28
00:02:40.039 --> 00:02:46.630
For supporting documents, older versions remain backed up in Google Drive and revised files go into a new submission folder.

29
00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:52.157
For CSV data, the old records are backed up in Google Sheets before the current records are overwritten.

30
00:02:52.157 --> 00:02:57.365
This preserves earlier versions for reference while allowing the current submission to be updated.

31
00:02:58.065 --> 00:03:07.861
The solution connects Google Apps Script for workflow and validation, Google Sheets for structured records and backups, and Google Drive for documents and folder permissions.

32
00:03:07.861 --> 00:03:12.646
It demonstrates portal development, institutional reporting, and review coordination.

33
00:03:12.646 --> 00:03:15.686
The accompanying case study explains the full process.

34
00:03:15.686 --> 00:03:20.865
No confidential records, working credentials, or unverified time-saving claims are included.
